  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Now that the FOXML and \"Fedora METS Extension\" formats have been versioned to 1.1, the server allows ingest and export of only the new formats.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "The 1.0 serializers/deserializers still exist...they're just not configured in the base-fedora.fcfg.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "The first part of this item is just to enable them.  Add the necessary sections to the base fedora.fcfg (use the new URIs for the old formats instead of the old strings), and make sure we have at least one ingest/export system test for each of the old formats.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "The second part of this item is to make the client aware of the fact that the server can handle the old formats.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "WARNINGS: Even with the above changes, old-style disseminators will be ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "type": "strong"
        }
       ],
       "text": "lost",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "text": " on ingest.  Users should somehow be made aware of this (some combo of doc/server/client warnings)",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
